**Read:** [Introduction to Mining Engineering — Penn State MNG 230](../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2), the full handling, planning, and material-flow discussions; [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), complete applicable handling, sampling, and characterization material; [Wills’ Mineral Processing Technology — Wills and Finch, eighth edition](../sources/Wills-Mineral-Processing-Technology.lingua#r_02W7VCEB3274XY5AKSH9SGPV1A), chapter 2 in full and the relevant modeling sections, when available.

A stockpile or silo separates production times and changes the feed delivered to the next operation. Inventory is physical material with composition, size, moisture, thermal/reactive behavior, and an uncertain spatial distribution. A spreadsheet label does not guarantee the reclaim stream's properties.

Build a time-dependent mass and constituent account from receipts, withdrawals, losses, and measured inventory changes. Distinguish calculated mean composition from its distribution and sequence. A weighted-average grade ignores segregation, reclaim geometry, selective handling, and nonlinear processing response; averaging recoveries from separate tests may not predict processing of a blend.

Storage can change moisture, oxidation, surface condition, contamination, or self-heating potential. The effect depends on actual mineral/material chemistry, scale, exposure, and history. Preserve batch/domain identity and test how much information survives transfer between mine, stockpile, plant, and customer.

**Work:** reconstruct a documented storage/blending case and its measurement basis. Independently reconcile inventory and constituent totals across a selected period, quantify the effect of moisture or survey bias, and compare predicted versus observed reclaim variability. Propose a sampling and reclaim observation that could distinguish segregation from changing mine feed. Evaluate blend alternatives using the downstream response and quality constraints, not only the average assay.

**Continue:** [Connect process control with dynamics, measurements, and a defined operating purpose](Process-instruments-dynamics-control-and-observed-response.lingua#r_1H6VW5FKZ9SFGTSAKW6GC302ZP).

